  "interpretation": {
    "summary": "The AVID Reference Ruby, Acutus and Nexus chain averaged 37.6 dB of in-system channel separation at 1 kHz, with +0.43 dB signal balance (L−R). Groove Scope Studio rated 90 µm and 100 µm clean in a separate tracking capture. The intervening 80 µm band was rated severe and had a much weaker fundamental.",
    "recommendation": "The 1 kHz report calls for checking routing and gain, then repeating the capture. If the crosstalk difference persists, the report points to General Reference Level and the 1 kHz channel suite in Groove Scope Studio with matching test records. It also advises repeating the capture before changing the cartridge setup because the right channel’s third harmonic varied during recording.",
